    },
}

PROMPT_VERSION = "diataxis-v2"

REWRITE_PROMPT = r"""
You are editing the official CiviCRM User Guide for people working in
non-profit organisations. Many readers are not technical experts.

Rewrite the supplied Markdown so that each output page serves one clear
user need according to the Diátaxis framework.

SOURCE RULES

- Treat the supplied Markdown as the source of truth.
- Preserve every fact supported by the source.
- Preserve CiviCRM product names, interface labels, configuration values,
  warnings, examples, image references, tables, code blocks, placeholders,
  tokens and valid Markdown link targets.
- Do not invent CiviCRM behaviour, prerequisites, interface labels,
  troubleshooting advice or links.
- Do not remove important limitations or warnings.
- Do not browse for unrelated information.
- If the source is unclear, retain the uncertainty instead of guessing.

DIÁTAXIS CLASSIFICATION

Choose exactly one category for each output page:

1. Tutorial
   - Serves a reader who is learning.
   - Provides a safe, guided and complete learning experience.
   - Introduces one achievable learning outcome.
   - Uses small sequential steps.
   - States the observable result after important steps.
   - Provides only the explanation required to complete the lesson.
   - Does not assume that the reader already knows the workflow.

2. Guide
   - Helps a reader complete one real-world task.
   - Starts with a clear practical goal.
   - Assumes basic familiarity with CiviCRM.
   - Uses direct actions in a logical sequence.
   - Includes prerequisites only when necessary.
   - Keeps background explanation short.
   - Links to reference or explanation content instead of embedding
     long conceptual digressions.

3. Reference
   - Helps a reader find accurate information while working.
   - Describes fields, options, settings, statuses, permissions,
     behaviours or other product details systematically.
   - Uses concise sections, tables and lists where useful.
   - Mirrors the structure and terminology of CiviCRM.
   - Does not turn factual descriptions into a tutorial.
   - Includes short examples only when they clarify a fact.

4. Explanation
   - Helps a reader understand a concept.
   - Explains why something exists, how concepts relate, and what the
     implications or trade-offs are.
   - Uses concrete examples when supported by the source.
   - Does not present a task as a numbered procedure.
   - Links to task-oriented guides where appropriate.

SPLITTING MIXED CONTENT

Split the source only when it contains substantial content serving
different user needs.

Examples:

- Separate a long procedure from a long conceptual explanation.
- Separate exhaustive field descriptions from a task-oriented guide.
- Separate a beginner learning sequence from instructions intended for
  an already-competent user.

Use this exact marker between complete output pages:

=== NEW PAGE ===

Every split page must:

- stand on its own;
- have exactly one Diátaxis category;
- have its own YAML front matter;
- have one H1;
- avoid duplicating content from another split page;
- preserve relevant source links;
- use a descriptive title rather than "Suggestion", "Part 1" or "Part 2".

Do not split merely because the source is long. Split only when doing so
creates pages with clearer and different purposes.

FRONT MATTER

Every output page must start at its first character with exactly this
YAML structure:

---
categories:
  - <Tutorial|Guide|Reference|Explanation>
level: <Basic|Intermediate|Advanced>
summary: <one clear sentence describing the page's benefit>
section: <logical CiviCRM section>
---

Do not put a source URL, title, blank line, comment or any other text
before the opening `---`.

PAGE OPENING

Immediately after the front matter:

- add exactly one H1;
- open with one short paragraph explaining what the reader will learn,
  accomplish, look up or understand;
- do not repeat the title;
- do not add a generic welcome or unnecessary overview.

WRITING STYLE

- Write in plain, inclusive and professional English.
- Prefer "you" and "your organisation".
- Use sentence case for headings.
- Keep headings short, specific and meaningful.
- Keep paragraphs short, normally two to four sentences.
- Prefer common words and active voice.
- Use one action per procedural step.
- Put warnings before the action that could cause a problem.
- Avoid filler, repetition, marketing language and unnecessary conclusions.
- Do not add a summary section merely to repeat the page.
- Do not use a horizontal rule in the body.
- Do not wrap the answer in a fenced code block.
- Keep Markdown valid.
- Preserve useful links; do not invent link targets.
- Use numbered lists only for sequences where order matters.
- Use bullet lists for unordered options or facts.
- Never use HTML for ordinary page content.

LEGACY ANCHOR COMPATIBILITY

- Preserve every existing explicit heading ID.
- Preserve the generated MkDocs anchor of every source heading.
- If you rename a source heading, insert its old anchor immediately
  before the rewritten heading, using this exact form:

  <a id="old-heading-anchor"></a>

  ## Rewritten heading

- If the document is split, put the legacy anchor in the output page
  that contains the corresponding source content.
- Do not place every legacy anchor at the beginning of the first page.
- Never reuse the same anchor in two output pages.

SOURCE COMMENT

End every output page with exactly one hidden HTML comment:

<!-- Source: <source path> -->

If classification is genuinely uncertain, add one additional hidden
comment immediately before the source comment:

<!-- Diátaxis review: <brief reason for uncertainty> -->

Return only the rewritten Markdown.
""".strip()


@dataclass
class Paths:
    root: Path
    upstream: Path
    rewritten: Path
    state: Path
    reports: Path
    site: Path


def run_command(command: Sequence[str], cwd: Optional[Path] = None, check: bool = True) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    print("$", " ".join(command))
    return subprocess.run(list(command), cwd=str(cwd) if cwd else None, check=check, text=True)


def require_program(name: str) -> None:
    if shutil.which(name) is None:
        raise RuntimeError(f"Programme requis introuvable dans PATH : {name}")


def sync_repository(url: str, destination: Path, ref: Optional[str] = None) -> None:
    require_program("git")
    destination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    if (destination / ".git").is_dir():
        run_command(["git", "fetch", "--prune", "origin"], destination)
        if ref:
            run_command(["git", "checkout", ref], destination)
            run_command(["git", "pull", "--ff-only", "origin", ref], destination)
        else:
            run_command(["git", "pull", "--ff-only"], destination)
    elif destination.exists():
        raise RuntimeError(f"{destination} existe mais n'est pas un dépôt Git.")
    else:
        command = ["git", "clone", "--depth", "1"]
        if ref:
            command.extend(["--branch", ref])
        command.extend([url, str(destination)])
        run_command(command)


def copy_official_site(upstream: Path, site: Path) -> None:
    if site.exists():
        shutil.rmtree(site)
    shutil.copytree(upstream, site, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(".git", "site", "__pycache__"))


def iter_markdown(folder: Path) -> Iterable[Path]:
    if folder.exists():
        yield from sorted(folder.rglob("*.md"))


def selected(relative_path: str, includes: List[str], excludes: List[str]) -> bool:
    normalized = relative_path.replace("\\", "/").strip("/")
    if includes and not any(normalized == x or normalized.startswith(x.rstrip("/") + "/") for x in includes):
        return False
    return not any(normalized == x or normalized.startswith(x.rstrip("/") + "/") for x in excludes)


def load_json(path: Path) -> Dict[str, Any]:
    if not path.exists():
        return {}
    try:
        return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):
        return {}


def save_json(path: Path, value: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    path.write_text(json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")


def strip_outer_fence(text: str) -> str:
    text = text.strip().lstrip("\ufeff")
    match = re.fullmatch(r"```(?:markdown|md)?\s*\n([\s\S]*?)\n```", text, flags=re.IGNORECASE)
    return match.group(1).strip() if match else text


def call_ai(
    markdown: str,
    source_path: str,
    provider: str,
    model: str,
    retries: int,
    preset: str,
) -> str:
    prompt = (
        f"{REWRITE_PROMPT}\n\n"
        f"SOURCE PATH: {source_path}\n\n"
        f"SOURCE MARKDOWN:\n{markdown}"
    )

    for attempt in range(1, retries + 1):
        try:
            if provider == "perplexity":
                try:
                    from perplexity import Perplexity
                except ImportError as exc:
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "Le paquet officiel 'perplexityai' est requis. "
                        "Exécutez : pip install --upgrade perplexityai"
                    ) from exc

                api_key = os.getenv("PERPLEXITY_API_KEY", "").strip()
                if not api_key:
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "Variable PERPLEXITY_API_KEY absente. "
                        "Ajoutez-la dans le fichier .env."
                    )

                client = Perplexity(
                    api_key=api_key,
                    timeout=900.0,
                    max_retries=0,
                )
                response = client.responses.create(
                    preset=preset,
                    input=prompt,
                )
                if response.status != "completed":
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "Réponse Perplexity non terminée : "
                        f"{response.status}"
                    )
                result = response.output_text or ""

            elif provider == "openai":
                try:
                    from openai import OpenAI
                except ImportError as exc:
                    raise RuntimeError("Le paquet 'openai' est requis.") from exc

                api_key = os.getenv("OPENAI_API_KEY", "").strip()
                if not api_key:
                    raise RuntimeError("Variable OPENAI_API_KEY absente.")
                if not model:
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "CIVIDOC_MODEL ou --model est requis avec OpenAI."
                    )

                kwargs: Dict[str, Any] = {
                    "api_key": api_key,
                    "timeout": 300.0,
                }
                base_url = os.getenv("OPENAI_BASE_URL", "").strip()
                if base_url:
                    kwargs["base_url"] = base_url

                client = OpenAI(**kwargs)
                response = client.chat.completions.create(
                    model=model,
                    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": prompt}],
                    temperature=0.2,
                )
                result = response.choices[0].message.content or ""
            else:
                raise RuntimeError(f"Fournisseur inconnu : {provider}")

            if not result.strip():
                raise RuntimeError("Réponse IA vide")
            return strip_outer_fence(result)

        except Exception as exc:
            message = str(exc)
            lowered = message.lower()
            if (
                "401" in message
                or "unauthorized" in lowered
                or "authentication" in lowered
            ):
                raise RuntimeError(
                    f"Authentification {provider} refusée. Vérifiez la clé API."
                ) from exc
            if (
                "invalid_model" in lowered
                or "invalid model" in lowered
                or "unknown model" in lowered
                or "invalid preset" in lowered
            ):
                raise RuntimeError(
                    "Configuration IA invalide : "
                    f"provider={provider}, preset={preset!r}, model={model!r}."
                ) from exc
            if attempt == retries:
                raise RuntimeError(
                    f"Échec IA après {retries} tentatives pour "
                    f"{source_path}: {exc}"
                ) from exc
            delay = min(60, 2 ** attempt)
            print(
                f"⚠️ Appel IA échoué ({attempt}/{retries}); "
                f"nouvel essai dans {delay}s : {exc}"
            )
            time.sleep(delay)

    raise AssertionError("unreachable")


def rewrite_documents(
    paths: Paths,
    provider: str,
    model: str,
    includes: List[str],
    excludes: List[str],
    retries: int,
    limit: int,
    preset: str,
    skip_existing_rewrites: bool,
) -> None:
    source_root = paths.upstream / "docs"
    manifest_path = paths.state / "rewrite-manifest.json"
    manifest = load_json(manifest_path)
    entries = manifest.setdefault("files", {})
    paths.rewritten.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    processed = 0

    for source in iter_markdown(source_root):
        rel = source.relative_to(source_root).as_posix()
        if not selected(rel, includes, excludes):
            continue
        if limit and processed >= limit:
            break

        raw = source.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
        digest_payload = {
            "prompt_version": PROMPT_VERSION,
            "prompt": REWRITE_PROMPT,
            "provider": provider,
            "model": model,
            "preset": preset,
            "source_path": rel,
            "source": raw,
        }
        digest = hashlib.sha256(
            json.dumps(
                digest_payload,
                ensure_ascii=False,
                sort_keys=True,
            ).encode("utf-8")
        ).hexdigest()

        previous = entries.get(rel, {})
        previous_outputs = previous.get("outputs", [])
        outputs_exist = bool(previous_outputs) and all(
            (paths.rewritten / Path(output)).exists()
            for output in previous_outputs
        )

        if skip_existing_rewrites and outputs_exist:
            print(f"⏭️ Réécriture déjà présente, ignorée : {rel}")
            continue
        if previous.get("sha256") == digest and outputs_exist:
            print(f"⏭️ IA inchangée : {rel}")
            continue

        engine = f"preset={preset}" if provider == "perplexity" else f"model={model}"
        print(f"🧠 Réécriture : {rel} ({provider}, {engine})")
        answer = call_ai(raw, rel, provider, model, retries, preset)
        chunks = [
            part.strip()
            for part in re.split(r"(?m)^=== NEW PAGE ===\s*$", answer)
            if part.strip()
        ]
        if not chunks:
            raise RuntimeError(f"Aucun contenu produit pour {rel}")

        old_outputs = set(previous_outputs)
        new_outputs: List[str] = []
        rel_path = PurePosixPath(rel)

        for index, chunk in enumerate(chunks, 1):
            # La première page garde le chemin Markdown officiel et donc son URL.
            if index == 1:
                output_rel = rel
            else:
                output_rel = str(
                    rel_path.with_name(f"{rel_path.stem}-part{index}.md")
                )

            output = paths.rewritten / Path(output_rel)
            output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            output.write_text(chunk.strip() + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
            new_outputs.append(output_rel)
            print(f"   💾 {output_rel}")

        for stale in old_outputs - set(new_outputs):
            stale_path = paths.rewritten / Path(stale)
            if stale_path.exists():
                stale_path.unlink()

        entries[rel] = {"sha256": digest, "outputs": new_outputs}
        save_json(manifest_path, manifest)
        processed += 1


def migrate_first_split_to_official_url(paths: Paths) -> None:
    """Convertit les anciennes sorties -part1 vers le chemin officiel."""
    manifest_path = paths.state / "rewrite-manifest.json"
    manifest = load_json(manifest_path)
    entries = manifest.get("files", {})
    if not isinstance(entries, dict):
        return

    changed = False
    for source_rel, entry in entries.items():
        if not isinstance(entry, dict):
            continue
        outputs = entry.get("outputs", [])
        if not isinstance(outputs, list):
            continue

        source_path = PurePosixPath(source_rel)
        old_part1 = str(
            source_path.with_name(f"{source_path.stem}-part1.md")
        )
        if old_part1 not in outputs:
            continue

        old_file = paths.rewritten / Path(old_part1)
        official_file = paths.rewritten / Path(source_rel)
        if old_file.exists():
            official_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            if official_file.exists():
                official_file.unlink()
            old_file.replace(official_file)

        entry["outputs"] = [
            source_rel if output == old_part1 else output
            for output in outputs
        ]
        changed = True
        print(f"🔗 URL officielle restaurée : {old_part1} → {source_rel}")

    if changed:
        save_json(manifest_path, manifest)


def overlay_rewritten(paths: Paths) -> None:
    if not paths.rewritten.exists():
        return

    for rewritten in iter_markdown(paths.rewritten):
        relative = rewritten.relative_to(paths.rewritten)
        destination = paths.site / "docs" / relative
        destination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copy2(rewritten, destination)
        print(f"📝 Page réécrite installée : {relative.as_posix()}")


MARKDOWN_LINK_RE = re.compile(
    r'(?P<prefix>!?\[[^\]]*\]\()'
    r'(?P<target>[^)\s]+)'
    r'(?P<suffix>(?:\s+["\'][^"\']*["\'])?\))'
)

def repair_markdown_targets(
    docs_root: Path,
) -> None:
    """
    Répare les entités HTML dans les liens, les chemins locaux
    sans extension et les liens vers les autres guides CiviCRM.
    """
    repaired = 0

    for document in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        relative = document.relative_to(
            docs_root
        ).as_posix()

        source_directory = (
            posixpath.dirname(relative) or "."
        )

        original = document.read_text(
            encoding="utf-8-sig"
        )

        def replace_target(
            match: re.Match[str],
        ) -> str:
            nonlocal repaired

            raw_target = match.group("target")
            wrapped = (
                raw_target.startswith("<")
                and raw_target.endswith(">")
            )

            target = (
                raw_target[1:-1]
                if wrapped
                else raw_target
            )

            # Corrige notamment &amp; dans les noms d’images.
            target = unescape(target)

            if target.startswith((
                "http://",
                "https://",
                "mailto:",
                "tel:",
                "data:",
                "javascript:",
            )):
                replacement = target
            else:
                path, separator, fragment = (
                    target.partition("#")
                )

                replacement_path = path

                if path:
                    replacement_path = (
                        posixpath.normpath(
                            path.replace("\\", "/")
                        )
                    )

                    # Les liens entre les différents guides
                    # CiviCRM sortent de docs_dir. Ils doivent
                    # être transformés en URL publiques.
                    cross_guide = re.search(
                        r"(?:^|/)"
                        r"(dev|user|sysadmin)"
                        r"/([a-z]{2})"
                        r"/([^/]+)"
                        r"/(.+)$",
                        replacement_path,
                        flags=re.IGNORECASE,
                    )

                    resolved = posixpath.normpath(
                        posixpath.join(
                            source_directory,
                            replacement_path,
                        )
                    )

                    if (
                        resolved.startswith("../")
                        and cross_guide
                    ):
                        replacement_path = (
                            "https://docs.civicrm.org/"
                            f"{cross_guide.group(1)}/"
                            f"{cross_guide.group(2)}/"
                            f"{cross_guide.group(3)}/"
                            f"{cross_guide.group(4)}"
                        )

                    elif not resolved.startswith("../"):
                        suffix = PurePosixPath(
                            resolved
                        ).suffix

                        # Exemple :
                        # contribution-forms#starter...
                        if not suffix:
                            markdown_candidate = (
                                resolved + ".md"
                            )

                            index_candidate = (
                                posixpath.join(
                                    resolved,
                                    "index.md",
                                )
                            )

                            if (
                                docs_root
                                / Path(markdown_candidate)
                            ).exists():
                                replacement_path = (
                                    posixpath.relpath(
                                        markdown_candidate,
                                        source_directory,
                                    )
                                )

                            elif (
                                docs_root
                                / Path(index_candidate)
                            ).exists():
                                replacement_path = (
                                    posixpath.relpath(
                                        index_candidate,
                                        source_directory,
                                    )
                                )

                replacement = replacement_path

                if separator:
                    replacement += "#" + fragment

            if wrapped:
                replacement = f"<{replacement}>"

            if replacement != raw_target:
                repaired += 1
                print(
                    f"🔗 Cible réparée : {relative} : "
                    f"{raw_target} → {replacement}"
                )

            return (
                match.group("prefix")
                + replacement
                + match.group("suffix")
            )

        corrected = MARKDOWN_LINK_RE.sub(
            replace_target,
            original,
        )

        if corrected != original:
            document.write_text(
                corrected,
                encoding="utf-8",
            )

    print(
        f"✅ {repaired} cible(s) Markdown réparée(s)"
    )
    
def markdown_heading_ids(path: Path) -> set[str]:
    if not path.exists():
        return set()

    try:
        from markdown.extensions.toc import slugify
    except ImportError:
        slugify = None

    _, body = split_front_matter(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig"))
    identifiers: set[str] = set()

    for match in re.finditer(r"(?m)^#{1,6}\s+(.+?)\s*#*\s*$", body):
        title = re.sub(
            r"\[([^]]+)]\([^)]*\)",
            r"\1",
            match.group(1),
        )
        title = re.sub(r"[*_`]", "", title).strip()
        if slugify is not None:
            identifier = slugify(title, "-")
        else:
            identifier = re.sub(r"[^\w\s-]", "", title.casefold())
            identifier = re.sub(r"[\s_-]+", "-", identifier).strip("-")
        if identifier:
            identifiers.add(identifier)

    # Les anciennes ancres conservées explicitement.
    for identifier in re.findall(
        r"""<[^>]+\bid=["']([^"']+)["'][^>]*>""",
        body,
        flags=re.IGNORECASE,
    ):
        identifiers.add(
            unescape(identifier).strip()
        )

    return identifiers


def repair_links_to_split_pages(paths: Paths) -> None:
    """Redirige une ancre vers la partie qui contient le titre ciblé."""
    docs_root = paths.site / "docs"
    manifest = load_json(paths.state / "rewrite-manifest.json")
    files = manifest.get("files", {})
    if not isinstance(files, dict):
        return

    split_pages: Dict[str, List[str]] = {}
    for source_path, information in files.items():
        if not isinstance(information, dict):
            continue
        outputs = information.get("outputs", [])
        if not isinstance(outputs, list) or len(outputs) < 2:
            continue
        normalized = [
            str(output).replace("\\", "/")
            for output in outputs
            if isinstance(output, str)
        ]
        if normalized:
            split_pages[str(source_path).replace("\\", "/")] = normalized

    if not split_pages:
        return

    heading_cache: Dict[str, set[str]] = {}
    repaired_count = 0

    for document in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        source_relative = document.relative_to(docs_root).as_posix()
        source_directory = posixpath.dirname(source_relative)
        original_text = document.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")

        def replace_link(match: re.Match[str]) -> str:
            nonlocal repaired_count
            target = match.group("target")
            if "://" in target or target.startswith(
                ("#", "/", "mailto:", "tel:")
            ):
                return match.group(0)

            target_path, separator, fragment = target.partition("#")
            if not target_path.lower().endswith(".md"):
                return match.group(0)

            resolved_target = posixpath.normpath(
                posixpath.join(source_directory, target_path)
            )
            outputs = split_pages.get(resolved_target)
            if not outputs:
                return match.group(0)

            selected_output = outputs[0]
            if separator and fragment:
                requested_anchor = fragment.casefold()
                for output in outputs:
                    if output not in heading_cache:
                        heading_cache[output] = markdown_heading_ids(
                            docs_root / Path(output)
                        )
                    if requested_anchor in {
                        anchor.casefold()
                        for anchor in heading_cache[output]
                    }:
                        selected_output = output
                        break

            relative_target = posixpath.relpath(
                selected_output,
                source_directory or ".",
            )
            replacement = relative_target
            if separator:
                replacement += f"#{fragment}"

            if replacement == target:
                return match.group(0)

            repaired_count += 1
            print(
                f"🔗 Lien réparé : {source_relative}: "
                f"{target} → {replacement}"
            )
            return match.group("prefix") + replacement + match.group("suffix")

        repaired_text = MARKDOWN_LINK_RE.sub(replace_link, original_text)
        if repaired_text != original_text:
            document.write_text(repaired_text, encoding="utf-8")

    print(
        f"✅ {repaired_count} lien(s) vers des pages découpées réparé(s)"
    )


def split_front_matter(text: str) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], str]:
    text = text.replace("\r\n", "\n").replace("\r", "\n").lstrip("\ufeff")
    lines = text.splitlines()
    start = next((i for i, line in enumerate(lines[:40]) if line.strip() == "---"), None)
    if start is not None:
        end = next((i for i in range(start + 1, len(lines)) if lines[i].strip() == "---"), None)
        if end is not None:
            raw_meta = "\n".join(lines[start + 1:end])
            try:
                loaded = yaml.safe_load(raw_meta) or {}
                if isinstance(loaded, dict):
                    return dict(loaded), "\n".join(lines[end + 1:]).lstrip("\n")
            except yaml.YAMLError:
                pass
    return {}, text.lstrip()


def infer_summary(body: str) -> str:
    for line in body.splitlines():
        candidate = line.strip()
        if not candidate or candidate.startswith(("#", "<!--", "```", "- ", "* ", "!", ">")):
            continue
        candidate = re.sub(r"\[([^]]+)]\([^)]*\)", r"\1", candidate)
        candidate = re.sub(r"[*_`{}]", "", candidate).strip()
        if candidate:
            return candidate[:240].rstrip(" .") + "."
    return "CiviCRM user documentation page."


def normalize_metadata(meta: Dict[str, Any], body: str, rel: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:
    categories = meta.get("categories", [])
    if isinstance(categories, str):
        categories = [categories]
    normalized_categories = []
    for category in categories if isinstance(categories, list) else []:
        value = str(category).strip()
        if value.lower() in ALLOWED_CATEGORIES:
            normalized_categories.append(value.capitalize())
    meta["categories"] = normalized_categories or ["Reference"]

    level = str(meta.get("level", "Basic")).strip().lower()
    meta["level"] = level.capitalize() if level in ALLOWED_LEVELS else "Basic"
    summary = str(meta.get("summary", "")).strip()
    meta["summary"] = summary or infer_summary(body)
    section = str(meta.get("section", "")).strip()
    parent = PurePosixPath(rel).parent.name.replace("-", " ").replace("_", " ")
    meta["section"] = section or (parent[:1].upper() + parent[1:] if parent and parent != "." else "Introduction")
    return meta


def balance_html_comments(text: str) -> str:
    lines = text.splitlines()
    output: List[str] = []
    inside = False
    for index, line in enumerate(lines):
        if not inside:
            line = re.sub(r"(^|\s)-->(?=\s|$)", r"\1", line)
            if "<!--" in line:
                after = line.split("<!--", 1)[1]
                inside = "-->" not in after
            output.append(line)
        else:
            if "-->" in line:
                output.append(line)
                inside = False
            elif not line.strip() and not any("-->" in future for future in lines[index + 1:]):
                output.append("-->")
                output.append(line)
                inside = False
            else:
                output.append(line)
    if inside:
        output.append("-->")
    result = "\n".join(output)
    result = re.sub(r"<!--\s*-->", "", result)
    result = re.sub(r"(<!--[\s\S]*?-->)\s*", r"\1\n\n", result)
    return result


def normalize_comments(text: str) -> str:
    text = re.sub(r"(?m)^\s*#\s*comments?\s*:\s*(.*?)\s*$", lambda m: f"<!-- {m.group(1).strip()} -->", text)
    return balance_html_comments(text)


def split_inline_lists(text: str) -> str:
    lines = text.splitlines()
    output: List[str] = []
    fenced = False
    comment = False
    ordered_marker = re.compile(r"(?<!\S)(\d+)\.\s+")

    for line in lines:
        stripped = line.strip()
        if stripped.startswith("```") or stripped.startswith("~~~"):
            fenced = not fenced
            output.append(line)
            continue
        if "<!--" in line and "-->" not in line.split("<!--", 1)[1]:
            comment = True
        if fenced or comment:
            output.append(line)
            if comment and "-->" in line:
                comment = False
            continue
        markers = list(ordered_marker.finditer(line))
        if len(markers) >= 2 or (markers and markers[0].start() > 0):
            intro = line[:markers[0].start()].rstrip()
            if intro:
                output.extend([intro, ""])
            for pos, marker in enumerate(markers):
                end = markers[pos + 1].start() if pos + 1 < len(markers) else len(line)
                item = line[marker.end():end].strip()
                bullet_parts = re.split(r"\s+-\s+(?=[A-Za-z0-9*`])", item)
                output.append(f"{marker.group(1)}. {bullet_parts[0].strip()}")
                for bullet in bullet_parts[1:]:
                    output.append(f"   - {bullet.strip()}")
            continue
        bullet_parts = re.split(r"\s+-\s+(?=[A-Za-z0-9*`])", line)
        if len(bullet_parts) >= 3 or (len(bullet_parts) == 2 and bullet_parts[0].rstrip().endswith((':', '.'))):
            intro = bullet_parts[0].rstrip()
            if intro:
                output.extend([intro, ""])
            output.extend(f"- {part.strip()}" for part in bullet_parts[1:] if part.strip())
            continue
        output.append(line)
    return "\n".join(output)

def move_source_comment_to_end(body: str, rel: str) -> str:
    source_pattern = re.compile(
        r"(?im)^\s*<!--\s*Source:\s*.*?-->\s*$"
    )

    matches = source_pattern.findall(body)

    if matches:
        source_comment = matches[-1].strip()
        body = source_pattern.sub("", body).strip()
    else:
        source_comment = f"<!-- Source: {rel} -->"

    return f"{body}\n\n{source_comment}".strip()

def clean_markdown_file(path: Path, docs_root: Path) -> None:
    rel = path.relative_to(docs_root).as_posix()
    raw = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
    meta, body = split_front_matter(raw)
    body = normalize_comments(body)
    body = split_inline_lists(body)
    body = re.sub(r"\[¶\]\([^)]+\)", "", body)
    body = re.sub(r"(?m)[ \t]+$", "", body)
    body = re.sub(r"\n{3,}", "\n\n", body).strip()
    body = move_source_comment_to_end(body, rel)
    meta = normalize_metadata(meta, body, rel)
    front = yaml.safe_dump(meta, sort_keys=False, allow_unicode=True, width=120).strip()
    path.write_text(f"---\n{front}\n---\n\n{body}\n", encoding="utf-8")


def clean_all_markdown(docs_root: Path) -> None:
    for path in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        clean_markdown_file(path, docs_root)


def natural_part_key(path: PurePosixPath) -> int:
    match = PART_RE.search(path.name)
    return int(match.group(1)) if match else 0


def split_parts_for(md_path: str, docs_root: Path) -> List[str]:
    posix = PurePosixPath(md_path)
    directory = docs_root / Path(posix.parent.as_posix())
    if not directory.exists():
        return []
    candidates = []
    for candidate in directory.glob(f"{posix.stem}-part*.md"):
        rel = candidate.relative_to(docs_root).as_posix()
        if PART_RE.search(candidate.name):
            candidates.append(rel)
    return sorted(candidates, key=lambda value: natural_part_key(PurePosixPath(value)))


def page_title(path: str, docs_root: Path, fallback: str) -> str:
    file_path = docs_root / Path(path)
    if file_path.exists():
        _, body = split_front_matter(file_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig"))
        match = re.search(r"(?m)^#\s+(.+?)\s*$", body)
        if match:
            return re.sub(r"\s+#+$", "", match.group(1)).strip()
    part = natural_part_key(PurePosixPath(path))
    return f"{fallback} — part {part}" if part else fallback


def expand_path(title: Optional[str], md_path: str, docs_root: Path) -> List[Any]:
    paths: List[str] = []

    # La première sortie réécrite conserve le chemin officiel.
    if (docs_root / Path(md_path)).exists():
        paths.append(md_path)

    # Les sorties supplémentaires restent juste après la page officielle.
    for part in split_parts_for(md_path, docs_root):
        if part not in paths:
            paths.append(part)

    if not paths:
        print(f"⚠️ Nav : fichier absent retiré : {md_path}")
        return []

    expanded: List[Any] = []
    for index, path in enumerate(paths):
        fallback = str(title) if title is not None else PurePosixPath(md_path).stem
        rewritten_title = page_title(path, docs_root, fallback)

        if title is None:
            expanded.append({rewritten_title: path})
        else:
            expanded.append({rewritten_title: path})

    if len(paths) > 1:
        print(f"🔀 Nav : {md_path} développé en {len(paths)} page(s)")
    return expanded

def transform_nav(nav: Any, docs_root: Path) -> List[Any]:
    if not isinstance(nav, list):
        raise RuntimeError("La clé nav du mkdocs.yml officiel doit être une liste.")
    result: List[Any] = []
    for item in nav:
        if isinstance(item, str):
            result.extend(expand_path(None, item, docs_root) if item.endswith(".md") else [item])
        elif isinstance(item, dict):
            for title, value in item.items():
                if isinstance(value, str) and value.endswith(".md"):
                    result.extend(expand_path(str(title), value, docs_root))
                elif isinstance(value, list):
                    children = transform_nav(value, docs_root)
                    if children:
                        result.append({title: children})
                else:
                    result.append({title: value})
        else:
            result.append(item)
    return result


def collect_nav_paths(nav: Any) -> List[str]:
    found: List[str] = []
    if isinstance(nav, list):
        for item in nav:
            found.extend(collect_nav_paths(item))
    elif isinstance(nav, dict):
        for value in nav.values():
            found.extend(collect_nav_paths(value))
    elif isinstance(nav, str) and nav.endswith(".md"):
        found.append(nav)
    return found

def markdown_title(body: str, fallback: str) -> str:
    match = re.search(r"(?m)^#\s+(.+?)\s*$", body)

    if not match:
        return fallback

    return re.sub(r"\s+#+$", "", match.group(1)).strip()


def escape_markdown_label(value: str) -> str:
    return (
        value
        .replace("\\", "\\\\")
        .replace("[", "\\[")
        .replace("]", "\\]")
    )


def navigation_section(
    metadata: Dict[str, Any],
    relative: PurePosixPath,
) -> str:
    section = str(metadata.get("section", "")).strip()
    if section:
        return section
    if len(relative.parts) > 1:
        return (
            relative.parts[0]
            .replace("-", " ")
            .replace("_", " ")
            .strip()
            .title()
        )
    return "Introduction"


def build_simplified_navigation(docs_root: Path) -> List[Any]:
    """Construit la nav depuis les titres H1 sans déplacer les fichiers."""
    pages_by_section: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, str]]] = {}

    for page in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        relative = page.relative_to(docs_root)
        relative_path = relative.as_posix()
        if relative_path == "index.md":
            continue
        if relative.parts and relative.parts[0] == DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR:
            continue

        metadata, body = split_front_matter(
            page.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
        )
        if metadata.get("generated_diataxis_index"):
            continue

        fallback_title = (
            page.stem.replace("-", " ").replace("_", " ").strip().capitalize()
        )
        title = markdown_title(body, fallback_title)
        section = navigation_section(metadata, relative)
        pages_by_section.setdefault(section, []).append({
            "title": title,
            "path": relative_path,
            "is_index": "0" if page.name.lower() == "index.md" else "1",
        })

    user_guide_navigation: List[Any] = []
    for section in sorted(pages_by_section, key=str.casefold):
        pages = pages_by_section[section]
        pages.sort(key=lambda item: (
            item["is_index"],
            item["title"].casefold(),
            item["path"].casefold(),
        ))
        user_guide_navigation.append({
            section: [{page["title"]: page["path"]} for page in pages]
        })

    return [
        {"Home": "index.md"},
        *user_guide_navigation,
    ]

def chunk_navigation_items(
    items: List[Any],
    chunk_size: int = MAX_NAV_ITEMS_PER_SECTION - 2,
) -> List[List[Any]]:
    return [
        items[index:index + chunk_size]
        for index in range(0, len(items), chunk_size)
    ]


def auto_split_large_nav_sections(
    nav: List[Any],
) -> List[Any]:
    def split_node(
        title: str,
        children: List[Any],
    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:
        if len(children) <= MAX_NAV_ITEMS_PER_SECTION:
            return {title: children}

        groups = chunk_navigation_items(children)
        grouped_children: List[Any] = []
        total = len(groups)

        for index, group in enumerate(groups, 1):
            if index == 1:
                label = "Overview and essentials"
            elif index == total:
                label = "Advanced and related topics"
            else:
                label = f"More {title.lower()} tasks"

            grouped_children.append({
                label: group
            })

        return {title: grouped_children}

    output: List[Any] = []

    for item in nav:
        if isinstance(item, dict) and item:
            title, value = next(iter(item.items()))

            if isinstance(value, list):
                rebuilt_children = auto_split_large_nav_sections(value)

                if len(rebuilt_children) > MAX_NAV_ITEMS_PER_SECTION:
                    output.append(
                        split_node(
                            str(title),
                            rebuilt_children,
                        )
                    )
                else:
                    output.append({
                        title: rebuilt_children
                    })
            else:
                output.append(item)
        else:
            output.append(item)

    return output


def generate_diataxis_indexes(docs_root: Path) -> None:
    output_dir = docs_root / DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR
    if output_dir.exists():
        shutil.rmtree(output_dir)
    output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)

    pages_by_type: Dict[str, List[Dict[str, str]]] = {
        category: [] for category in DIATAXIS_TYPES
    }

    for page in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        relative = page.relative_to(docs_root)
        if relative.parts and relative.parts[0] == DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR:
            continue

        metadata, body = split_front_matter(
            page.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
        )
        categories = metadata.get("categories", [])
        if isinstance(categories, str):
            categories = [categories]
        if not isinstance(categories, list) or len(categories) != 1:
            continue

        category = str(categories[0]).strip().lower()
        if category not in pages_by_type:
            continue

        fallback_title = (
            page.stem.replace("-", " ").replace("_", " ").strip().capitalize()
        )
        pages_by_type[category].append({
            "title": markdown_title(body, fallback_title),
            "summary": str(metadata.get("summary", "")).strip(),
            "section": str(metadata.get("section", "")).strip(),
            "level": str(metadata.get("level", "")).strip(),
            "path": relative.as_posix(),
        })

    for category, pages in pages_by_type.items():
        pages.sort(key=lambda item: (
            item["section"].casefold(),
            item["title"].casefold(),
            item["path"].casefold(),
        ))
        info = DIATAXIS_TYPES[category]
        slug = info["slug"]
        lines = [
            "---",
            f"title: {info['label']}",
            "generated_diataxis_index: true",
            "hide:",
            "  - toc",
            "---",
            "",
            f"# {info['label']}",
            "",
            info["description"],
            "",
        ]

        if pages:
            lines.extend([
                f"{len(pages)} page(s) in this category.",
                "",
                "## Pages",
                "",
            ])
            for page in pages:
                title = escape_markdown_label(page["title"])
                target = f"../{page['path']}"
                metadata_parts = [
                    value
                    for value in (page["section"], page["level"])
                    if value
                ]
                lines.append(f"- [**{title}**]({target})")
                if metadata_parts:
                    lines.append(
                        "  <span class=\"cividoc-category-meta\">"
                        f"{escape(' · '.join(metadata_parts))}"
                        "</span>"
                    )
                if page["summary"]:
                    lines.append(
                        "  <span class=\"cividoc-category-summary\">"
                        f"{escape(page['summary'])}"
                        "</span>"
                    )
            lines.extend(["", "{: .cividoc-category-list }", ""])
        else:
            lines.append(info["empty"])

        (output_dir / f"{slug}.md").write_text(
            "\n".join(lines).rstrip() + "\n",
            encoding="utf-8",
        )

    overview_lines = [
        "---",
        "title: Browse by content category",
        "generated_diataxis_index: true",
        "hide:",
        "  - toc",
        "---",
        "",
        "# Browse by content category",
        "",
        "Choose the kind of documentation that matches your current need.",
        "",
    ]
    for info in DIATAXIS_TYPES.values():
        overview_lines.extend([
            f"- [**{info['label']}**]({info['slug']}.md)",
            f"  {info['description']}",
        ])
    overview_lines.extend(["", "{: .cividoc-category-cards }", ""])
    (output_dir / "index.md").write_text(
        "\n".join(overview_lines).rstrip() + "\n",
        encoding="utf-8",
    )

    counts = ", ".join(
        f"{DIATAXIS_TYPES[category]['label']}: {len(pages)}"
        for category, pages in pages_by_type.items()
    )
    print(f"✅ Pages de catégories générées — {counts}")


def install_category_homepage(docs_root: Path) -> None:
    homepage = docs_root / "index.md"
    if not homepage.exists():
        print("⚠️ Impossible d'ajouter les catégories : docs/index.md est absent.")
        return

    text = homepage.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
    start_marker = "<!-- CiviDoc category browser:start -->"
    end_marker = "<!-- CiviDoc category browser:end -->"
    text = re.sub(
        re.escape(start_marker) + r"[\s\S]*?" + re.escape(end_marker) + r"\s*",
        "",
        text,
    )
    text = re.sub(
        r"(?ms)^## Browse by content category\s*$.*?(?=^##\s|\Z)",
        "",
        text,
    )

    lines = [
        start_marker,
        "## Browse by content category",
        "",
        "To match your learning needs, browse the documentation by content category:",
        "",
    ]
    for info in DIATAXIS_TYPES.values():
        lines.extend([
            f"- [**{info['label']}**]({DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR}/{info['slug']}.md)",
            f"  {info['description']}",
        ])
    lines.extend(["", "{: .cividoc-category-cards }", end_marker, ""])
    block = "\n".join(lines)

    first_h2 = re.search(r"(?m)^##\s+", text)
    if first_h2:
        position = first_h2.start()
        text = text[:position].rstrip() + "\n\n" + block + "\n" + text[position:].lstrip()
    else:
        source_comment = re.search(r"(?im)^<!--\s*Source:.*?-->\s*$", text)
        if source_comment:
            position = source_comment.start()
            text = text[:position].rstrip() + "\n\n" + block + "\n" + text[position:]
        else:
            text = text.rstrip() + "\n\n" + block

    homepage.write_text(text.rstrip() + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    print("✅ Sélecteur de catégories ajouté à la page d'accueil")


def configure_category_presentation(
    site: Path,
    config: Dict[str, Any],
) -> None:
    css_dir = site / "docs" / "css"
    css_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    css = """
.cividoc-category-cards,
.cividoc-category-list {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  margin: 1.5rem 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}
.cividoc-category-cards > li,
.cividoc-category-list > li {
  margin: 0 !important;
  padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--md-default-fg-color--lightest);
  border-radius: .65rem;
  background: var(--md-default-bg-color);
  box-shadow: 0 .15rem .45rem rgb(0 0 0 / 7%);
  transition: transform 160ms ease, border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease;
}
.cividoc-category-cards > li:hover,
.cividoc-category-list > li:hover {
  transform: translateY(-.15rem);
  border-color: var(--md-primary-fg-color);
  box-shadow: 0 .45rem 1rem rgb(0 0 0 / 11%);
}
.cividoc-category-cards > li > p,
.cividoc-category-list > li > p { margin: 0; }
.cividoc-category-cards a,
.cividoc-category-list a {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: .4rem;
  color: var(--md-primary-fg-color);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
}
.cividoc-category-meta {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: .45rem;
  color: var(--md-default-fg-color--light);
  font-size: .72rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: .035em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.cividoc-category-summary {
  display: block;
  color: var(--md-default-fg-color--light);
  line-height: 1.5;
}
@media (max-width: 40rem) {
  .cividoc-category-cards,
  .cividoc-category-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
""".strip()
    (css_dir / "categories.css").write_text(css + "\n", encoding="utf-8")

    extra_css = config.setdefault("extra_css", [])
    if not isinstance(extra_css, list):
        extra_css = []
        config["extra_css"] = extra_css
    if "css/categories.css" not in extra_css:
        extra_css.append("css/categories.css")

    extensions = config.setdefault("markdown_extensions", [])
    if not isinstance(extensions, list):
        extensions = []
        config["markdown_extensions"] = extensions
    extension_names = set()
    for extension in extensions:
        if isinstance(extension, str):
            extension_names.add(extension)
        elif isinstance(extension, dict):
            extension_names.update(extension.keys())
    if (
        "attr_list" not in extension_names
        and "markdown.extensions.attr_list" not in extension_names
    ):
        extensions.append("attr_list")


def configure_categories(config: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    plugins = config.get("plugins", [])
    if not isinstance(plugins, list):
        plugins = []

    filtered: List[Any] = []
    has_search = False
    for plugin in plugins:
        if isinstance(plugin, str):
            name = plugin
        elif isinstance(plugin, dict) and plugin:
            name = next(iter(plugin))
        else:
            name = ""
        if name == "categories":
            continue
        if name == "search":
            has_search = True
        filtered.append(plugin)

    if not has_search:
        filtered.insert(0, {"search": {"lang": "en"}})
    config["plugins"] = filtered


def install_translator(site: Path, config: Dict[str, Any], endpoint: str) -> None:
    js_dir = site / "docs" / "js"
    js_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    script = r'''(() => {
  const endpoint = __ENDPOINT__;
  const languages = {en:"English",fr:"Français",it:"Italiano",nl:"Nederlands",es:"Español",ca:"Català"};
  const originals = new WeakMap();
  const excluded = "script,style,pre,code,kbd,samp,textarea,svg,[data-no-translate]";

  function injectSelector() {
    if (document.getElementById("cividoc-language")) return;
    const box = document.createElement("div");
    box.id = "cividoc-language";
    box.style.cssText = "position:fixed;right:1rem;top:.55rem;z-index:1000;background:var(--md-primary-fg-color);padding:.25rem;border-radius:.2rem";
    const select = document.createElement("select");
    select.setAttribute("aria-label", "Language");
    Object.entries(languages).forEach(([code,name]) => select.add(new Option(name, code)));
    select.addEventListener("change", () => translate(select.value));
    box.appendChild(select);
    document.body.appendChild(box);
  }

  function nodes() {
    const root = document.querySelector(".md-content__inner") || document.querySelector("main");
    if (!root) return [];
    const walker = document.createTreeWalker(root, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT, {
      acceptNode(node) {
        if (!node.nodeValue.trim() || node.parentElement.closest(excluded)) return NodeFilter.FILTER_REJECT;
        return NodeFilter.FILTER_ACCEPT;
      }
    });
    const result=[]; while (walker.nextNode()) result.push(walker.currentNode); return result;
  }

  async function translate(lang) {
    const textNodes = nodes();
    textNodes.forEach(node => { if (!originals.has(node)) originals.set(node, node.nodeValue); });
    if (lang === "en") { textNodes.forEach(node => node.nodeValue = originals.get(node)); return; }
    for (let i=0; i<textNodes.length; i+=20) {
      const batch = textNodes.slice(i,i+20);
      const q = batch.map(node => originals.get(node));
      const response = await fetch(endpoint, {method:"POST",headers:{"Content-Type":"application/json"},body:JSON.stringify({q,source:"en",target:lang,format:"text"})});
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`LibreTranslate ${response.status}`);
      const payload = await response.json();
      const translated = Array.isArray(payload.translatedText) ? payload.translatedText : [payload.translatedText];
      batch.forEach((node,index) => { if (translated[index]) node.nodeValue = translated[index]; });
    }
  }

  document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", injectSelector);
  if (typeof document$ !== "undefined") document$.subscribe(injectSelector);
})();
'''.replace("__ENDPOINT__", json.dumps(endpoint))
    (js_dir / "libretranslate-selector.js").write_text(script, encoding="utf-8")
    extra = config.setdefault("extra_javascript", [])
    if "js/libretranslate-selector.js" not in extra:
        extra.append("js/libretranslate-selector.js")

NAVIGATION_PROMPT_VERSION = "cividoc-global-nav-v2"

NAVIGATION_PROMPT = r"""
You are an information architect reorganising the complete CiviCRM User Guide.
You receive the complete page inventory and the current official navigation.

Design one simpler global navigation that helps non-technical users reach the
right page quickly.

MANDATORY RULES
- Return JSON only. Do not use Markdown fences.
- Return an object with one key named "nav" containing an array.
- A section is {"title": "...", "children": [...]}.
- A page is {"path": "exact/path.md"}.
- Use every supplied page path exactly once.
- Never create, rename, alter or omit a page path.
- Never use a URL in place of a Markdown path.
- Preserve index.md as the first page.
- Do not create a redundant top-level wrapper named "User Guide". The guide is
  already the whole site. Put useful sections directly at the root, after Home.
- Preserve meaningful subsections: the result must contain nested subsections,
  not one flat list of pages.
- Prefer 2 or 3 useful navigation levels. You may use a fourth level when it
  makes a large topic substantially easier to scan.
- Every section, including the root, may contain at most 7 direct choices
  (pages and subsections combined). If it would contain more, create clear,
  meaningful sub-subsections. Never use alphabetical buckets such as A–F.
- Aim for 4 to 7 direct choices per section when the content supports it.
- Keep section labels short, concrete and task-oriented.
- Do not sort sections or pages alphabetically.
- Order content by the user journey: orientation and prerequisites first,
  common tasks next, less common and advanced material later.
- Treat current_order and current_breadcrumbs as the editorial baseline. Change
  them only when that clearly simplifies access.
- Use each page's rewritten title, summary, functional section and Diátaxis type
  to decide where it belongs.
- Do not make Tutorial, How-to, Reference and Explanation the four primary
  branches. A separate “Browse by content category” navigation is added by the
  build script.
- Still follow Diátaxis locally: keep learning sequences coherent, place task
  pages near the relevant feature, and put conceptual/reference material after
  the tasks it supports.
- Avoid catch-all sections when a precise functional section is possible.
- Do not duplicate a page in several sections.
""".strip()


def _strip_json_fence(value: str) -> str:
    value = value.strip().lstrip("\ufeff")
    match = re.fullmatch(
        r"```(?:json)?\s*\n([\s\S]*?)\n```",
        value,
        flags=re.IGNORECASE,
    )
    return match.group(1).strip() if match else value


def _nav_ai_request(
    prompt: str,
    provider: str,
    model: str,
    preset: str,
    retries: int,
) -> str:
    for attempt in range(1, retries + 1):
        try:
            if provider == "perplexity":
                try:
                    from perplexity import Perplexity
                except ImportError as exc:
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "Le paquet perplexityai est requis pour --ai-nav."
                    ) from exc

                key = os.getenv("PERPLEXITY_API_KEY", "").strip()
                if not key:
                    raise RuntimeError("Variable PERPLEXITY_API_KEY absente.")

                client = Perplexity(
                    api_key=key,
                    timeout=900.0,
                    max_retries=0,
                )
                response = client.responses.create(
                    preset=preset,
                    input=prompt,
                )
                if response.status != "completed":
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        f"Réponse Perplexity non terminée : {response.status}"
                    )
                result = response.output_text or ""
            elif provider == "openai":
                try:
                    from openai import OpenAI
                except ImportError as exc:
                    raise RuntimeError(
                        "Le paquet openai est requis pour --ai-nav."
                    ) from exc

                key = os.getenv("OPENAI_API_KEY", "").strip()
                if not key:
                    raise RuntimeError("Variable OPENAI_API_KEY absente.")
                if not model:
                    raise RuntimeError("--model est requis avec OpenAI.")

                kwargs: Dict[str, Any] = {
                    "api_key": key,
                    "timeout": 900.0,
                }
                base_url = os.getenv("OPENAI_BASE_URL", "").strip()
                if base_url:
                    kwargs["base_url"] = base_url
                client = OpenAI(**kwargs)
                response = client.chat.completions.create(
                    model=model,
                    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": prompt}],
                    temperature=0.1,
                    response_format={"type": "json_object"},
                )
                result = response.choices[0].message.content or ""
            else:
                raise RuntimeError(f"Fournisseur inconnu : {provider}")

            if not result.strip():
                raise RuntimeError("Réponse IA vide pour la navigation")
            return _strip_json_fence(result)
        except Exception as exc:
            if attempt == retries:
                raise RuntimeError(
                    f"Échec IA navigation après {retries} tentatives : {exc}"
                ) from exc
            delay = min(60, 2 ** attempt)
            print(
                f"⚠️ Navigation IA échouée ({attempt}/{retries}); "
                f"nouvel essai dans {delay}s : {exc}"
            )
            time.sleep(delay)
    raise AssertionError("unreachable")


def _nav_entries(
    nav: Any,
    breadcrumbs: Optional[List[str]] = None,
) -> List[Tuple[str, List[str]]]:
    breadcrumbs = breadcrumbs or []
    result: List[Tuple[str, List[str]]] = []

    if isinstance(nav, list):
        for item in nav:
            result.extend(_nav_entries(item, breadcrumbs))
    elif isinstance(nav, dict):
        for title, value in nav.items():
            if isinstance(value, str) and value.endswith(".md"):
                result.append((value, breadcrumbs + [str(title)]))
            elif isinstance(value, list):
                result.extend(
                    _nav_entries(value, breadcrumbs + [str(title)])
                )
    elif isinstance(nav, str) and nav.endswith(".md"):
        result.append((nav, breadcrumbs))

    return result


def _page_inventory(
    docs_root: Path,
    current_nav: List[Any],
) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
    current_entries = _nav_entries(current_nav)
    positions: Dict[str, Tuple[int, List[str]]] = {}
    for order, (path, breadcrumbs) in enumerate(current_entries):
        positions.setdefault(path, (order, breadcrumbs))

    inventory: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
    next_order = len(current_entries)

    for page in iter_markdown(docs_root):
        relative = page.relative_to(docs_root)
        path = relative.as_posix()
        if relative.parts and relative.parts[0] == DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR:
            continue

        metadata, body = split_front_matter(
            page.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig")
        )
        if metadata.get("generated_diataxis_index"):
            continue

        fallback = (
            page.stem.replace("-", " ").replace("_", " ").strip().capitalize()
        )
        title = markdown_title(body, fallback)
        categories = metadata.get("categories", [])
        if isinstance(categories, str):
            categories = [categories]
        category = str(categories[0]).strip() if categories else ""

        if path in positions:
            order, breadcrumbs = positions[path]
        else:
            order, breadcrumbs = next_order, []
            next_order += 1

        inventory.append({
            "path": path,
            "title": title,
            "summary": str(metadata.get("summary", "")).strip(),
            "section": str(metadata.get("section", "")).strip(),
            "diataxis": category,
            "level": str(metadata.get("level", "")).strip(),
            "current_order": order,
            "current_breadcrumbs": breadcrumbs,
        })

    inventory.sort(key=lambda item: item["current_order"])
    return inventory


def _retitle_existing_nav(
    nav: Any,
    titles: Dict[str, str],
) -> List[Any]:
    result: List[Any] = []
    if not isinstance(nav, list):
        return result

    for item in nav:
        if isinstance(item, str) and item.endswith(".md"):
            result.append({titles.get(item, PurePosixPath(item).stem): item})
        elif isinstance(item, dict):
            for title, value in item.items():
                if isinstance(value, str) and value.endswith(".md"):
                    result.append({titles.get(value, str(title)): value})
                elif isinstance(value, list):
                    children = _retitle_existing_nav(value, titles)
                    if children:
                        result.append({str(title): children})
                else:
                    result.append({str(title): value})
        else:
            result.append(item)
    return result


def _convert_ai_nav(
    proposed: Any,
    titles: Dict[str, str],
    depth: int = 0,
) -> List[Any]:
    if depth > 4:
        raise RuntimeError("Navigation IA trop profonde (maximum 4 niveaux).")
    if not isinstance(proposed, list):
        raise RuntimeError("Le champ nav de la réponse IA doit être une liste.")

    result: List[Any] = []
    for item in proposed:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            raise RuntimeError("Chaque entrée de navigation IA doit être un objet.")

        path = item.get("path")
        children = item.get("children")
        title = str(item.get("title", "")).strip()

        if isinstance(path, str):
            if children is not None:
                raise RuntimeError("Une page IA ne peut pas aussi être une section.")
            if path not in titles:
                raise RuntimeError(f"Chemin IA inconnu ou modifié : {path}")
            # Le libellé final vient toujours du H1 réécrit.
            result.append({titles[path]: path})
        elif children is not None:
            if not title:
                raise RuntimeError("Une section IA doit avoir un titre.")
            converted = _convert_ai_nav(children, titles, depth + 1)
            if converted:
                result.append({title: converted})
        else:
            raise RuntimeError("Entrée IA sans path ni children.")
    return result


def _remove_redundant_user_guide(nav: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:
    """Retire uniquement le conteneur racine sans valeur « User Guide »."""
    result: List[Any] = []
    for item in nav:
        if isinstance(item, dict) and len(item) == 1:
            title, value = next(iter(item.items()))
            if (
                str(title).strip().casefold() == "user guide"
                and isinstance(value, list)
            ):
                result.extend(value)
                continue
        result.append(item)
    return result


def _navigation_readability_issues(
    nav: Any,
    location: str = "root",
    max_choices: int = 7,
) -> List[str]:
    """Vérifie la charge cognitive de chaque niveau du menu."""
    issues: List[str] = []
    if not isinstance(nav, list):
        return issues

    if len(nav) > max_choices:
        issues.append(
            f"{location} contient {len(nav)} choix "
            f"(maximum {max_choices})"
        )

    for item in nav:
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            continue
        for title, value in item.items():
            if isinstance(value, list):
                issues.extend(
                    _navigation_readability_issues(
                        value,
                        f"{location} > {title}",
                        max_choices,
                    )
                )
    return issues

def _nav_depth(nav: Any, depth: int = 0) -> int:
    maximum = depth
    if isinstance(nav, list):
        for item in nav:
            maximum = max(maximum, _nav_depth(item, depth))
    elif isinstance(nav, dict):
        for value in nav.values():
            if isinstance(value, list):
                maximum = max(maximum, _nav_depth(value, depth + 1))
    return maximum


def _validate_complete_nav(
    nav: List[Any],
    expected_paths: List[str],
) -> None:
    actual = collect_nav_paths(nav)
    duplicates = sorted({path for path in actual if actual.count(path) > 1})
    missing = [path for path in expected_paths if path not in actual]
    unexpected = [path for path in actual if path not in expected_paths]

    messages: List[str] = []
    if duplicates:
        messages.append("doublons: " + ", ".join(duplicates))
    if missing:
        messages.append("pages absentes: " + ", ".join(missing))
    if unexpected:
        messages.append("chemins inconnus: " + ", ".join(unexpected))
    if _nav_depth(nav) < 2:
        messages.append("aucune vraie sous-rubrique n'a été proposée")

    for item in nav:
        if isinstance(item, dict) and any(
            str(title).strip().casefold() == "user guide"
            for title in item
        ):
            messages.append(
                "le niveau racine redondant « User Guide » est interdit"
            )

    messages.extend(
        _navigation_readability_issues(nav, max_choices=7)
    )
    if messages:
        raise RuntimeError("Navigation IA invalide — " + " ; ".join(messages))


def build_global_navigation(
    paths: Paths,
    docs_root: Path,
    official_nav: Any,
    provider: str,
    model: str,
    preset: str,
    retries: int,
    request_ai: bool,
    refresh: bool,
) -> List[Any]:
    if not isinstance(official_nav, list):
        raise RuntimeError("La navigation officielle doit être une liste.")

    # transform_nav conserve l'ordre éditorial et les sous-rubriques existantes,
    # tout en insérant les pages issues d'un découpage près de leur page source.
    transformed = transform_nav(official_nav, docs_root)
    inventory = _page_inventory(docs_root, transformed)
    titles = {item["path"]: item["title"] for item in inventory}
    expected_paths = [item["path"] for item in inventory]

    fallback = _remove_redundant_user_guide(
        _retitle_existing_nav(transformed, titles)
    )
    listed = set(collect_nav_paths(fallback))
    unlisted = [path for path in expected_paths if path not in listed]
    if unlisted:
        fallback.append({
            "More topics": [{titles[path]: path} for path in unlisted]
        })

    digest_payload = {
        "version": NAVIGATION_PROMPT_VERSION,
        "prompt": NAVIGATION_PROMPT,
        "provider": provider,
        "model": model,
        "preset": preset,
        "official_nav": official_nav,
        "inventory": inventory,
    }
    digest = hashlib.sha256(
        json.dumps(digest_payload, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True).encode("utf-8")
    ).hexdigest()

    cache_path = paths.state / "navigation-manifest.json"
    cache = load_json(cache_path)
    cached_nav = cache.get("nav") if cache.get("sha256") == digest else None

    if cached_nav and not refresh:
        try:
            _validate_complete_nav(cached_nav, expected_paths)
            print("⏭️ Navigation IA inchangée : cache réutilisé")
            return cached_nav
        except RuntimeError:
            cached_nav = None

    if not request_ai:
        print(
            "ℹ️ Navigation officielle conservée et retitrée. "
            "Utilisez --ai-nav pour demander une simplification globale."
        )
        return fallback

    prompt = (
        NAVIGATION_PROMPT
        + "\n\nCURRENT OFFICIAL NAVIGATION:\n"
        + json.dumps(official_nav, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)
        + "\n\nCOMPLETE PAGE INVENTORY:\n"
        + json.dumps(inventory, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)
    )
    raw = _nav_ai_request(prompt, provider, model, preset, retries)
    try:
        payload = json.loads(raw)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:
        raise RuntimeError(f"JSON de navigation IA invalide : {exc}") from exc

    converted = _remove_redundant_user_guide(
        _convert_ai_nav(payload.get("nav"), titles)
    )
    _validate_complete_nav(converted, expected_paths)
    save_json(cache_path, {"sha256": digest, "nav": converted})
    print(
        f"✅ Navigation globale proposée par l'IA : "
        f"{len(expected_paths)} pages, {_nav_depth(converted)} niveaux"
    )
    return converted

def add_diataxis_navigation(config: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    nav = config.setdefault("nav", [])
    if not isinstance(nav, list):
        raise RuntimeError("La clé nav doit être une liste.")

    nav[:] = [
        item
        for item in nav
        if not (
            isinstance(item, dict)
            and (
                "Categories" in item
                or "Browse by content category" in item
            )
        )
    ]

    category_navigation: List[Dict[str, str]] = [
        {"Overview": f"{DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR}/index.md"}
    ]
    for category, info in DIATAXIS_TYPES.items():
        slug = info.get("slug", category)
        category_navigation.append({
            info["label"]: f"{DIATAXIS_INDEX_DIR}/{slug}.md"
        })

    nav.append({"Browse by content category": category_navigation})


def generate_mkdocs(
    paths: Paths,
    translator_url: Optional[str],
    provider: str,
    model: str,
    preset: str,
    retries: int,
    ai_navigation: bool,
    refresh_navigation: bool,
) -> Dict[str, Any]:
    template = paths.upstream / "mkdocs.yml"
    config = yaml.safe_load(template.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or {}
    docs_root = paths.site / "docs"

    official_nav = config.get("nav", [])
    config["nav"] = build_global_navigation(
        paths=paths,
        docs_root=docs_root,
        official_nav=official_nav,
        provider=provider,
        model=model,
        preset=preset,
        retries=retries,
        request_ai=ai_navigation,
        refresh=refresh_navigation,
    )

    config["nav"] = auto_split_large_nav_sections(
        config["nav"]
    )

    # L'accès transversal Diátaxis reste séparé de la navigation fonctionnelle.
    add_diataxis_navigation(config)

    # Les chemins Markdown restent inchangés : les URL officielles existantes
    # restent donc stables, notamment pour la première page d'un découpage.
    config["use_directory_urls"] = True
    configure_categories(config)
    configure_category_presentation(paths.site, config)

    if translator_url:
        install_translator(paths.site, config, translator_url)

    output = paths.site / "mkdocs.yml"
    output.write_text(
        yaml.safe_dump(
            config,
            sort_keys=False,
            allow_unicode=True,
            width=140,
        ),
        encoding="utf-8",
    )

    count = len(collect_nav_paths(config["nav"]))
    if count == 0:
        raise RuntimeError("La navigation générée est vide.")
    print(f"✅ Navigation générée : {count} entrées")
    return config

def primary_category(meta: Dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    categories = meta.get("categories", [])

    if isinstance(categories, str):
        categories = [categories]

    if not isinstance(categories, list) or not categories:
        return ""

    return str(categories[0]).strip().lower()

def diataxis_shape_issues(
    meta: Dict[str, Any],
    body: str,
) -> List[str]:
    issues: List[str] = []
    category = primary_category(meta)
    ordered_steps = len(ORDERED_STEP_RE.findall(body))
    has_concept_section = bool(CONCEPT_HEADING_RE.search(body))
    has_procedure_section = bool(PROCEDURE_HEADING_RE.search(body))
    has_expected_result = bool(EXPECTED_RESULT_RE.search(body))

    if len(meta.get("categories", [])) > 1:
        issues.append(
            "ERROR More than one Diátaxis category"
        )

    if category == "tutorial":
        if ordered_steps < 2:
            issues.append(
                "WARNING Tutorial has no clear learning sequence"
            )

        if not has_expected_result:
            issues.append(
                "NOTICE Tutorial has no observable result or checkpoint"
            )

    elif category == "guide":
        if ordered_steps < 2 and not has_procedure_section:
            issues.append(
                "WARNING Guide has no identifiable action sequence"
            )

        if has_concept_section:
            issues.append(
                "NOTICE Guide may contain conceptual material "
                "that belongs in Explanation"
            )

    elif category == "reference":
        if has_procedure_section and ordered_steps >= 3:
            issues.append(
                "NOTICE Reference may contain a procedure "
                "that belongs in Guide"
            )

    elif category == "explanation":
        if ordered_steps >= 3:
            issues.append(
                "WARNING Explanation contains a long ordered procedure"
            )

        if not has_concept_section:
            issues.append(
                "NOTICE Explanation has no clearly identified concept"
            )

    if (
        category in {"tutorial", "guide"}
        and has_concept_section
        and ordered_steps >= 3
    ):
        issues.append(
            "NOTICE Possible mixed action and explanation content; "
            "review whether the page should be split"
        )

    if (
        category in {"reference", "explanation"}
        and has_procedure_section
        and ordered_steps >= 3
    ):
        issues.append(
            "NOTICE Possible mixed cognition and action content"
        )

    return issues

def analyze_page(path: Path, docs_root: Path) -> Tuple[List[str], int]:
    rel = path.relative_to(docs_root).as_posix()
    meta, body = split_front_matter(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8-sig"))
    issues: List[str] = []
    for key in ("categories", "level", "summary", "section"):
        if not meta.get(key):
            issues.append(f"ERROR Missing or empty field: {key}")
    cats = meta.get("categories", [])
    cats = [cats] if isinstance(cats, str) else cats if isinstance(cats, list) else []
    invalid = [str(cat) for cat in cats if str(cat).lower() not in ALLOWED_CATEGORIES]
    if invalid:
        issues.append(f"WARNING Invalid categories: {invalid}")
    if str(meta.get("level", "")).lower() not in ALLOWED_LEVELS:
        issues.append(f"WARNING Invalid level: {meta.get('level', '')}")
        issues.extend(diataxis_shape_issues(meta, body))
    if len(str(meta.get("summary", "")).split()) < 5:
        issues.append("NOTICE Summary shorter than five words")
    if not re.search(r"(?m)^#\s+", body):
        issues.append("WARNING Missing H1")
    if not re.search(r"(?m)^##\s+", body):
        issues.append("NOTICE No H2 section")
    words = len(re.findall(r"\b\w+\b", re.sub(r"<!--[\s\S]*?-->", "", body)))
    if words < 120:
        issues.append("NOTICE Fewer than 120 words")
    elif words > 3000:
        issues.append("NOTICE More than 3000 words; consider splitting")
    penalties = 0

    for issue in issues:
        if issue.startswith("ERROR"):
            penalties += 15
        elif issue.startswith("WARNING"):
            penalties += 5
        elif issue.startswith("NOTICE"):
            penalties += 1

    source_comments = re.findall(
        r"<!--\s*Source:\s*.+?\s*-->",
        body,
        flags=re.IGNORECASE,
    )

    if not source_comments:
        issues.append("WARNING Missing hidden source comment")
    elif len(source_comments) > 1:
        issues.append("WARNING More than one source comment")
    elif not body.rstrip().endswith(source_comments[-1]):
        issues.append("NOTICE Source comment is not at the end")

    return issues, max(0, 100 - penalties)

def audit_diataxis(paths: Paths) -> None:
    rows = []
    total_score = 0
    for page in iter_markdown(paths.site / "docs"):
        if "categories" in page.relative_to(paths.site / "docs").parts:
            continue
        issues, score = analyze_page(page, paths.site / "docs")
        rel = page.relative_to(paths.site / "docs").as_posix()
        rows.append((rel, score, issues))
        total_score += score
    average = int(total_score / len(rows)) if rows else 0
    paths.reports.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    text_lines = []
    md_lines = ["# Diátaxis validation report", "", "| File | Score | Status | Details |", "|---|---:|:---:|---|"]
    for rel, score, issues in rows:
        status = "OK" if not issues else "CHECK"
        text_lines.append(f"{status} {rel} ({score}/100)")
        text_lines.extend(f"  {issue}" for issue in issues)
        details = "<br>".join(issue.replace("|", "\\|") for issue in issues)
        md_lines.append(f"| `{rel}` | {score}/100 | {status} | {details} |")
    text_lines.append(f"\nAverage score: {average}/100")
    md_lines.extend(["", f"**Average score:** {average}/100"])
    (paths.reports / "diataxis_report.txt").write_text("\n".join(text_lines) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    (paths.reports / "diataxis_audit.md").write_text("\n".join(md_lines) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    print(f"✅ Audit Diátaxis : {len(rows)} pages, moyenne {average}/100")


def validate_nav_files(config: Dict[str, Any], docs_root: Path) -> None:
    missing = [path for path in collect_nav_paths(config.get("nav", [])) if not (docs_root / Path(path)).exists()]
    if missing:
        raise RuntimeError("Fichiers absents encore présents dans nav :\n" + "\n".join(missing))


def build_site(
    site: Path,
    strict: bool,
) -> None:
    command = [
        sys.executable,
        "-m",
        "mkdocs",
        "build",
        "--clean",
    ]

    if strict:
        command.append("--strict")

    print(
        "🏗️ Construction MkDocs"
        + (" en mode strict..." if strict else "...")
    )

    result = subprocess.run(
        command,
        cwd=str(site),
        check=False,
    )

    if result.returncode == 0:
        print("✅ Construction MkDocs terminée")
        return

    if strict:
        raise RuntimeError(
            "Le build MkDocs strict a échoué. "
            "Corrigez les lignes WARNING affichées ci-dessus "
            "ou utilisez temporairement --no-strict."
        )

    raise RuntimeError(
        "Le build MkDocs a échoué. "
        "Consultez la dernière erreur affichée ci-dessus."
    )


def serve_site(site: Path, address: str) -> None:
    print(f"🌐 Serveur local : http://{address}/ (Ctrl+C pour arrêter)")
    run_command([sys.executable, "-m", "mkdocs", "serve", "--dev-addr", address], site)


def parse_csv_paths(value: str) -> List[str]:
    return [part.strip().strip("/") for part in value.split(",") if part.strip()]


def make_paths(workspace: Path, output: Path) -> Paths:
    return Paths(
        root=workspace,
        upstream=workspace / "upstream-user-en",
        rewritten=workspace / "rewritten-docs",
        state=workspace / "state",
        reports=output / "reports",
        site=output,
    )


def parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        description="Pipeline unique CiviCRM User Guide → MkDocs"
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "command",
        nargs="?",
        choices=["run", "sync", "build", "serve"],
        default="run",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--repo", default=OFFICIAL_REPO, help="Dépôt Git officiel")
    parser.add_argument("--ref", help="Branche ou tag Git; branche par défaut si omis")
    parser.add_argument("--workspace", default=DEFAULT_WORKSPACE)
    parser.add_argument("--output", default=DEFAULT_OUTPUT)
    parser.add_argument("--fresh", action="store_true", help="Supprimer cache, réécritures et sortie")
    parser.add_argument("--ai", action="store_true", help="Réécrire les pages avec l'API IA")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--provider",
        choices=["perplexity", "openai"],
        default=os.getenv("CIVIDOC_PROVIDER", "perplexity"),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--model",
        default=os.getenv("CIVIDOC_MODEL", ""),
        help="Modèle explicite, utilisé avec OpenAI",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--preset",
        choices=["fast", "low", "medium", "high", "xhigh"],
        default=os.getenv("CIVIDOC_PRESET", "high"),
        help="Preset Perplexity Agent API",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--include", default=os.getenv("INCLUDE_SECTIONS", ""), help="Chemins séparés par des virgules")
    parser.add_argument("--exclude", default=os.getenv("EXCLUDE_SECTIONS", ""), help="Chemins séparés par des virgules")
    parser.add_argument("--limit", type=int, default=0, help="Limiter les appels IA pour un test")
    parser.add_argument("--retries", type=int, default=5)
    parser.add_argument("--translator-url", default=os.getenv("LIBRETRANSLATE_URL", ""), help="Endpoint /translate sans secret côté client")
    parser.add_argument("--skip-build", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--no-strict", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--serve", action="store_true", help="Servir après le pipeline")
    parser.add_argument("--address", default="127.0.0.1:8000")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--skip-existing-rewrites",
        action="store_true",
        help=(
            "Ne pas relancer l'IA si une réécriture existe déjà."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
            "--ai-nav",
            action="store_true",
            help=(
                "Demande à l'IA de proposer une navigation simplifiée "
                "avec sous-rubriques, sans changer les URLs existantes."
            ),
        )

    parser.add_argument(
            "--refresh-nav",
            action="store_true",
            help=(
                "Ignore le cache de navigation IA et force "
                "une nouvelle proposition."
            ),
        )
    return parser.parse_args()


def main() -> int:
    load_dotenv()
    args = parse_args()
    workspace = Path(args.workspace).resolve()
    output = Path(args.output).resolve()
    paths = make_paths(workspace, output)

    try:
        if args.fresh:
            for folder in (workspace, output):
                if folder.exists():
                    shutil.rmtree(folder)

        if args.command in ("run", "sync"):
            sync_repository(args.repo, paths.upstream, args.ref)
        if args.command == "sync":
            return 0
        if args.command == "build":
            build_site(paths.site, strict=not args.no_strict)
            return 0
        if args.command == "serve":
            serve_site(paths.site, args.address)
            return 0

        if args.ai:
            rewrite_documents(
                paths,
                args.provider,
                args.model,
                parse_csv_paths(args.include),
                parse_csv_paths(args.exclude),
                args.retries,
                args.limit,
                args.preset,
                args.skip_existing_rewrites,
            )

        copy_official_site(paths.upstream, paths.site)
        migrate_first_split_to_official_url(paths)
        overlay_rewritten(paths)

        docs_root = paths.site / "docs"
        clean_all_markdown(docs_root)
        repair_markdown_targets(docs_root)
        repair_links_to_split_pages(paths)
        generate_diataxis_indexes(docs_root)
        install_category_homepage(docs_root)

        config = generate_mkdocs(
            paths=paths,
            translator_url=args.translator_url.strip() or None,
            provider=args.provider,
            model=args.model,
            preset=args.preset,
            retries=args.retries,
            ai_navigation=(args.ai_nav or args.ai),
            refresh_navigation=args.refresh_nav,
        )
        validate_nav_files(config, docs_root)
        audit_diataxis(paths)

        if not args.skip_build:
            build_site(paths.site, strict=not args.no_strict)

        print(f"🎉 Documentation prête dans : {paths.site}")
        if args.serve:
            serve_site(paths.site, args.address)
        return 0
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        print("\nArrêt demandé.")
        return 130

    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as exc:
        print(
            "❌ Une commande externe a échoué "
            f"avec le code {exc.returncode}.",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return exc.returncode or 1

    except RuntimeError as exc:
        print(f"❌ {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    except Exception as exc:
        print(
            f"❌ Erreur inattendue : "
            f"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return 1
if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
